{47}{Other questions!}{}{-4}{}{25}{}
{49}{The Derian-Ka was the ancient Order of the Dead, formed by the disciples of the great necromancer, Kerghan, in the years following his banishment.  They were a secret society, unknown for years, who practiced the arts of Dark Necromancy...}{The Derian-Ka was the ancient Order of the Dead, formed by the disciples of the great necromancer, Kerghan, in the years following his banishment.  They were a secret society, unknown for years, who practiced the arts of Dark Necromancy...}{}{8}{}{}
{50}{Why was it so secret?  What were they doing?}{}{5}{pa 6577, lf5 0}{56}{lf5 1}
{51}{Why was it so secret?  What were they doing?}{}{5}{pa -6577, lf5 0}{60}{}
{52}{Why was it so secret?  What were they doing?}{}{5}{pa 6577, lf5 1}{56}{lf5 1}
{53}{Why was it so secret?  What were they doing?}{}{5}{pa -6577, lf5 1}{60}{}
{54}{Why so secret?  They do bad things?}{}{-4}{}{60}{}
{56}{[He looks at Geoffrey, bowing slightly.]  Perhaps you should ask your companion.  He is of the Derian-Ka...I can sense it.  Greetings, sir...}{[He looks at Geoffrey, bowing slightly.]  Perhaps you should ask your companion.  He is of the Derian-Ka...I can sense it.  Greetings, sir...}{}{9}{}{}
{57}{Uh...Geoffrey?  What's he talking about...?}{}{5}{}{-13}{}
{60}{Perhaps things are different now, but the practice of the dark necromantic arts was forbidden for many years.  The Derian-Ka lived among the shadows for centuries, wielding their dark magicks behind locked doors, uncovering the secrets of the spirit worlds...soul-poisons, the raising of the undead [He points to himself.], speaking with spirits beyond the grave...}{Perhaps things are different now, but the practice of the dark necromantic arts was forbidden for many years.  The Derian-Ka lived among the shadows for centuries, wielding their dark magicks behind locked doors, uncovering the secrets of the spirit worlds...soul-poisons, the raising of the undead [He points to himself.], speaking with spirits beyond the grave...}{}{10}{}{}
{61}{What happened to them? }{}{5}{}{64}{}
{62}{Whut happen to them?}{}{-4}{}{64}{}
{64}{There was a great schism in the Order.  Within the  Derian-Ka were an order of assassins.  They were called the Molochean Hand, and for centuries they were the silent weapon of the Derian-Ka, a deadly defense against the world and its prejudices.  But one day the Hand turned against the Order, and there was war between them...}{There was a great schism in the Order.  Within the  Derian-Ka were an order of assassins.  They were called the Molochean Hand, and for centuries they were the silent weapon of the Derian-Ka, a deadly defense against the world and its prejudices.  But one day the Hand turned against the Order, and there was war between them...}{}{11}{}{}
{65}{And so?  What caused the schism...?}{}{5}{}{68}{}
{66}{Uh...whut happened to Hand?}{}{-4}{}{68}{}
{68}{I never knew what happened to cause that rift.  But because of it, the Gray Legions were raised...}{I never knew what happened to cause that rift.  But because of it, the Gray Legions were raised...}{}{12}{}{}
{69}{What were the Gray Legions?}{}{5}{}{74}{}
{70}{Whut the 'Gr-ray Le-j-j-uns'?}{}{-4}{}{74}{}
{71}{K:}{}{1}{}{37}{}
{72}{E:}{}{1}{}{0}{}
{74}{The Gray Legions were a great army of the undead, raised by the Derian-Ka as protection against the Molochean Hand.  Our sole purpose was to eradicate all traces of the Hand, so that the Order could continue...}{The Gray Legions were a great army of the undead, raised by the Derian-Ka as protection against the Molochean Hand.  Our sole purpose was to eradicate all traces of the Hand, so that the Order could continue...}{}{13}{}{}
{75}{You spoke of a great battle?}{}{5}{}{80}{}
{76}{You said you in a big battle...?}{}{-4}{}{80}{}
{77}{K:}{}{1}{}{37}{}
{78}{E:}{}{1}{}{0}{}
{80}{[Torian Kel seems lost in thought, his eyes somewhere far away.]  10,000 strong we were, fearless and of one mind.  Standing upon that battle-field, the darkened sky reflected in our black, burnished Dread-Armor...the stamping cavalry on their Shadow Stallions behind the endless rows of the stone-faced pikemen.  It was cold, but we had no breath...the air was so still...}{[Torian Kel seems lost in thought, his eyes somewhere far away.]  10,000 strong we were, fearless and of one mind.  Standing upon that battle-field, the darkened sky reflected in our black, burnished Dread-Armor...the stamping cavalry on their Shadow Stallions behind the endless rows of the stone-faced pikemen.  It was cold, but we had no breath...the air was so still...}{}{14}{}{}
{81}{And the Hand?}{}{5}{}{84}{}
{82}{Whut about Mo-o-l-lok-e-un H-a-nnd?}{}{-4}{}{84}{}
{84}{The Hand?  Yes, the Hand...[A look of pain, regret.]  The Hand were the greatest warriors of their time.  Quick, deadly, precise.  They stood across from us, on the opposite ridge.  Lightly armored, faces masked...their archers armed with Elven Great Bows, almost as tall as they were.  [His voice is a whisper.]  And fire, stranger, so much fire...}{The Hand?  Yes, the Hand...[A look of pain, regret.]  The Hand were the greatest warriors of their time.  Quick, deadly, precise.  They stood across from us, on the opposite ridge.  Lightly armored, faces masked...their archers armed with Elven Great Bows, almost as tall as they were.  [His voice is a whisper.]  And fire, stranger, so much fire...}{}{15}{}{}
{85}{And there was a battle?}{}{5}{}{88}{}
{86}{Did you fight them?}{}{-4}{}{88}{}
{88}{Oh yes...there was a battle the likes of which Arcanum had never seen, perhaps will never see again.  The Hand threw themselves against us, we without death, time and time again.  They severed the arm that held the sword, burned the body which held the arm, destroyed the souls within those bodies...the Hand, you see, were themselves not unlearned in the ways of magick...}{Oh yes...there was a battle the likes of which Arcanum had never seen, perhaps will never see again.  The Hand threw themselves against us, we without death, time and time again.  They severed the arm that held the sword, burned the body which held the arm, destroyed the souls within those bodies...the Hand, you see, were themselves not unlearned in the ways of magick...}{}{16}{}{}
{89}{And the Gray Legions were defeated?}{}{5}{}{92}{}
{90}{Hand beat the Gray Lejuns?}{}{-4}{}{92}{}
{92}{Yes...the Gray Legions fell on that day, but so did many of the Molochean Hand.  A few soldiers from both armies stumbled off the battlefield, and were lost to history.  The Derian-Ka were never heard from again...}{Yes...the Gray Legions fell on that day, but so did many of the Molochean Hand.  A few soldiers from both armies stumbled off the battlefield, and were lost to history.  The Derian-Ka were never heard from again...}{}{17}{}{lf1 1}
{93}{You said you were 'the last'...what did that mean?}{}{5}{}{98}{}
{94}{Uh...you say 'the last'...}{}{-4}{}{98}{}
{95}{K:}{}{1}{}{37}{}
{96}{E:}{}{1}{}{0}{}
{98}{As I said, there were a few Gray Legionnaires who survived.  Because we were undead, we walked Arcanum for centuries, trying to stay hidden from the eyes of man.  But the flesh, even the flesh of the undead, cannot last forever.  Little by little, year by year, our earthly shells decayed...}{As I said, there were a few Gray Legionnaires who survived.  Because we were undead, we walked Arcanum for centuries, trying to stay hidden from the eyes of man.  But the flesh, even the flesh of the undead, cannot last forever.  Little by little, year by year, our earthly shells decayed...}{}{18}{}{}
{99}{Hence, why you were a skeleton a few moments ago...}{}{5}{}{102}{}
{100}{That's why you wuz a skeleton!}{}{-4}{}{102}{}
{102}{Yes...and I was fortunate.  Do you see the piles of dust scattered here and there?  Those are the last remains of my companions.  Dead, but not dead...you see, their souls are still trapped here on this plane.  Forever tied to their earthly remains.  A curse...a cruel, cruel curse...}{Yes...and I was fortunate.  Do you see the piles of dust scattered here and there?  Those are the last remains of my companions.  Dead, but not dead...you see, their souls are still trapped here on this plane.  Forever tied to their earthly remains.  A curse...a cruel, cruel curse...}{}{19}{}{}
{103}{Is there nothing to be done?}{}{5}{}{106}{}
{104}{Whut can you do?}{}{-4}{}{106}{}
{106}{There is nothing I can do.  The Dragon's Blood pool can restore the flesh, but even it has its limits.  Nothing will ever raise my comrades from the dust.  They will live on...without voice, without dreams, without vision...}{There is nothing I can do.  The Dragon's Blood pool can restore the flesh, but even it has its limits.  Nothing will ever raise my comrades from the dust.  They will live on...without voice, without dreams, without vision...}{}{20}{}{lf3 1}
{107}{What will you do now, Torian?}{}{5}{}{117}{}
{108}{Whut you gonna do now, Toreun?}{}{-4}{}{117}{}
